<title>USA: Optical Sensors wins Europe certification.</title>
<headline>Optical Sensors wins Europe certification.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Optical Sensors Inc on Wednesday said it received the European Medical Directive &quot;CE&quot; mark, which it can now place on its medical products sold outside the United States.</p>
<p>The designation is part of a system for registering medical devices in Europe, allowing the products to be marketed freely in both the European Union and the European Free Trade Association, the company said.</p>
<p>Optical Sensors makes systems for monitoring blood gases.</p>
<p>Its shares closed down 1/8 at 10-3/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
